    },
    {
      "id": "TZwIl",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,&nbsp;<math><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;are the length of sides of triangle, then we know that the sum of two sides of a triangle is more than the third side i.e.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math></p><p><math><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>The discriminant of the quadratic&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and we know that if the discriminant of a quadratic is negative and its leading coefficient is positive then the quadratic is positive for all real numbers.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math></p><p><math><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8746;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, taking intersection of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Out of the given options only&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is not in the interval obtained.</p></blockquote>",
